-- title:
--   Weight 2 or p+1 at level N' traded for weight 2 at level N'p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ whose $p$-torsion is residually irreducible in the sense of `ModRepIsIrreducible`: the $p$-torsion subgroup of the points of $W$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole group. Let $N' \neq 0$ with $p \nmid N'$, and assume $3 < p$ or $3 < N'$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals containing $p$, every prime divisor of $N'$ and every prime $q$ with $q \mid \Delta_W$. Let $k = 2$ or $k = p+1$. Write $\mathbb{T}(M,k)$ for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S_0$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S_0$. Suppose $\mathfrak{m}_k \subset \mathbb{T}(N',k)$ is a maximal ideal containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a_\ell$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$, where $a_\ell = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$. Then there is a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2 \subset \mathbb{T}(N'p,2)$ containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a_\ell$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'p$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$.
--
--   This is the weight-to-level trade for Hecke eigensystems attached to $W$ (Ribet's Theorem 2.2 in his report on mod $\ell$ representations), converting an eigensystem maximal ideal in weight $2$ or $p+1$ at level prime to $p$ into one in weight $2$ at level $N'p$. It feeds the residual modularity statement [`WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_isNewform_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_two_dvd_of_eq_three`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_div_of_isNewform_of_inertia_moves_torsion_of_two_dvd_of_eq_three); the case $k = 2$ is handled by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two).
